  #line-at(153.12pt, 147.93pt, "In solid-state nanopores, achieving reliable control over pore aperture opening and closing (gating) remains a major ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 159.95pt, "challenge. Gating can be driven by the applied voltage involving electrically tunable chemical reactions, achieved by selecting ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 171.95pt, "appropriate compounds within the nanopore volume. In particular, cyclic precipitation and dissolution of metal phosphates ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 183.95pt, "can be triggered by regulating cation transport through an applied transmembrane voltage, thereby enabling reversible pore ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 195.95pt, "gating. Under negative bias, metal phosphate precipitates form inside the pore, obstructing ion flow and reducing current. ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 207.97pt, "Switching the polarity dissolves the precipitates, restoring ionic conductance. This process effectively produces a nanofluidic ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 219.97pt, "diode characterized by a remarkably high rectification ratio. To probe these localized chemical reactions more directly, we ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 231.97pt, "employed a plasmonic nanopore that generates strong confined fields, enabling surface-enhanced Raman scattering (SERS) ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 243.97pt, "measurements within the nanopore volume during cyclic gating. These measurements not only validate the proposed in-")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 256pt, "pore chemistry but also highlight the potential of plasmonic nanopores as powerful tools for monitoring nanoscale chemical ")
  #line-at(153.12pt, 268pt, "processes with high spatial resolution.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12.394pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 289.85pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.619pt, 301.88pt, "Over the past two decades, solid-state nanopore technology ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 313.88pt, "has been the focus of extensive research, particularly aimed at ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 325.88pt, "creating artificial systems that mimic biological nanopores—")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 337.88pt, "transmembrane proteins capable of regulating the passage of ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 349.9pt, "individual molecules and ions")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(161.26pt, 346.9pt, "1–4")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.12pt, 349.9pt, ". While the primary effort has ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 361.9pt, "traditionally centered on sequencing applications—initially for ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 373.9pt, "single DNA molecules and more recently for single proteins ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.64pt, 370.9pt, "5–")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 382.9pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.881pt, 385.9pt, "—the scope of interest in nanopore systems has now expanded ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 397.93pt, "considerably. Among various research directions, the use of ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 409.93pt, "solid-state nanopores for constructing nanofluidic circuits—")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 421.93pt, "such as ionic transistors and diodes—has recently attracted ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 433.95pt, "significant attention ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.81pt, 430.93pt, "2,10–12")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.26pt, 433.95pt, ". To develop a nanofluidic ionic ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 445.95pt, "system that mimics the behavior of a diode, precise control over ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 457.95pt, "the nanopore’s geometry and surface charge is essential. This is ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 469.95pt, "because ion selectivity, the key mechanism to be exploited, ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 481.97pt, "cannot be effectively achieved with conventional Si")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(244.02pt, 482.83pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(247.48pt, 481.97pt, "N")
