  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303.64pt, 276.14pt, "We showed that such diode-like behaviour of the nanopore system ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 288.14pt, "is due to the formation of a solid precipitate via V")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(484.21pt, 289pt, "b")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(487.21pt, 288.14pt, "-derived reactions ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 300.16pt, "that occluded the space for the electromigration of ions through the ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 312.16pt, "pores. Hence, we are observing precipitation reactions between ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 324.16pt, "divalent cations with the phosphoric acid in the electrolyte buffer to ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 336.16pt, "form metal phosphates. This can be understood considering the ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 348.19pt, "components in our chamber. The main ionic components of PBS in ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 360.19pt, "water are: Na⁺ , Cl⁻ , HPO₄²⁻ and H₂PO₄⁻ (the phosphate buffer pair). ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 372.19pt, "A divalent cloride compond in acqueous solution dissolves as : XCl₂ ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 384.19pt, "(s) → X²⁺ (aq) + 2Cl⁻ (aq), where X represents here Ca and Mn. ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 396.21pt, "Calcium and Manganese ions (X")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(434.88pt, 393.21pt, "2+")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.88pt, 396.21pt, ") are known to react with ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 408.21pt, "phosphate ions to form insoluble phosphate salts, with a pH ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 420.21pt, "dependent reaction:  ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 444.24pt, "3X²⁺+2PO₄³⁻→X₃(PO₄)₂  ")
  #line-at(519.81pt, 444.24pt, "(1) ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 468.24pt, "In PBS, most phosphate is present as HPO₄²⁻ or H₂PO₄⁻, but under ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 480.26pt, "physiological pH, there is still sufficient PO₄³⁻ to trigger partial ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 492.26pt, "precipitation of salts phosphate (especially hydroxyapatite or ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 504.26pt, "amorphous X–P compounds). Therefore, the following reaction most ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 516.26pt, "likely happens at the interface between Cis and Trans sides (the ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 528.28pt, "nanopore’s volume):  ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 552.28pt, "3XCl₂ +2Na₃PO₄ →X₃(PO₄)₂ +6NaCl  ")
  #line-at(519.81pt, 552.28pt, "(2) ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 576.31pt, "This reaction is strongly pH dependent as also demonstrated in our ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 588.31pt, "previour experiments")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(383.43pt, 585.31pt, "15")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(389.86pt, 588.31pt, ", and therefore we use PBS at physiological ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 600.31pt, "pH. ")
]

