  #line-at(209.29pt, 417.21pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(215.74pt, 420.21pt, ". This enables the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 432.21pt, "monitoring of the reaction inside the nanopore. In order to ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 444.24pt, "avoid the background signal from the PBS solution in the Trans ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 456.24pt, "volume, we excited the pore from the Cis side where only the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 468.24pt, "chloride salts are present. Testing both a single nanopore and ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 480.26pt, "an array of 16 pores (prepared in close proximity) it was not ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 492.26pt, "possible to detect convincing spectra to be ascribed to the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 504.26pt, "precipitated salts. This because the volume of detection is ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 516.26pt, "spatially limited by the nanopore’s diameter. While with the dry ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 528.28pt, "precipitates we can collect the signals from large area and large ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 540.28pt, "volume samples, here it has not been possible to obtain enough ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 552.28pt, "photons from the excited materials. This is the main motivation ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 564.28pt, "for the choice of the plasmonic nanopore. In fact, replicating the ")
