  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303.64pt, 502.12pt, "In summary, this work demonstrates the advantages of ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 514.12pt, "plasmonic nanopore approach for probing nanoscale chemical ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 526.14pt, "processes. By confining intense electromagnetic fields to the ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 538.14pt, "attoliter-scale volume within a pore, the system achieves ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 550.14pt, "enhanced spatiotemporal resolution for monitoring localized ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 562.14pt, "chemical reactions via the ionic current. Simultaneously, SERS ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 574.16pt, "signals from the plasmonic hotspot provide molecular ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 586.16pt, "vibrational signatures that serve as rich chemical “fingerprints” ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 598.16pt, "of the reactants and products. This synergy between label-free ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 610.16pt, "electrical and optical readouts enables real-time in situ analysis ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 622.19pt, "of dynamic nanoscale chemical processes that are inaccessible ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 634.19pt, "to conventional analytical tools. ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 646.19pt, "Beyond validating the specific in-pore precipitation/dissolution ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 658.19pt, "reaction, the strengths demonstrated here translate into broad ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 670.21pt, "practical applications across chemistry and biotechnology. In ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 682.21pt, "biosensing, a plasmonic nanopore can serve as a single-")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 694.21pt, "molecule analytical tool capable of identifying biomolecules ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 706.21pt, "such as proteins or nucleic acids by their vibrational spectra ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 718.24pt, "without the need for fluorescent or enzymatic labels, thereby ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 730.24pt, "enabling rapid diagnostics and sequencing. In catalytic reaction ")
  #line-at(303.64pt, 742.235pt, "monitoring and synthetic chemistry, this platform allows ")
]

