  #line-at(42.452pt, 84.04pt, "reaction kinetics as they occur. Such real-time insights into ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 96.04pt, "reaction pathways can inform catalyst design and process ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 108.04pt, "optimization and might even enable the discovery of novel ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 120.07pt, "reaction intermediates or products. By exploiting the nanopore ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 132.07pt, "as a nanoreactor with finely tunable conditions, one could ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 144.07pt, "potentially synthesize new compounds that are challenging to ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 156.07pt, "produce in bulk solution. Overall, this approach could transform ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 168.09pt, "how we study and control nanoscale chemistry, offering ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 180.09pt, "unprecedented ")
  #line-at(118.628pt, 180.09pt, "spatiotemporal ")
  #line-at(194.39pt, 180.09pt, "resolution, ")
  #line-at(252.206pt, 180.09pt, "molecular ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 192.09pt, "specificity, and operando monitoring capabilities for next-")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 204.09pt, "generation biosensors, catalysts, and nanofluidic devices. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 262.43pt, "Materials and methods ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.857pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 279.14pt, "Nanopore fabrication ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.619pt, 295pt, "Free standing SiN membrane chips were fabricated using a ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 307.02pt, "standard MEMS procesure based on commercial double-sided ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 319.02pt, "100 nm LPCVD SiN-coated 500 μm silicon wafer. On on side, an ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 331.02pt, "array of ~850 μm SiN squres with 5mm periods was defined by ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 343.04pt, "UV photolithography (S1813), after RIE ething the SiN with CHF")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(288.64pt, 343.9pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 355.04pt, "and O")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(68.19pt, 355.9pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(71.19pt, 355.04pt, ", the wafer was cleaned by acetone and O2 plasma ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 367.04pt, "before soak into 32% KOH solution under 90 degree for few ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 379.04pt, "hours to to remove the silicon inside the UV lithography difined ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 391.07pt, "window thus make the other side SiN a suspended membrane. ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 403.07pt, "After sputter 5/30 nm Ti/Au on top of the SiN membrane, 18 pA ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 415.07pt, "focused ion beam (FIB, FEI 650) with 30 kV accelerate speed was ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 427.07pt, "used to drill ~ 200 nm pore and Au bullseye nanostructures ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 439.09pt, "around the pore. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.857pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 463.09pt, "Ionic current measurements  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(42.452pt, 475.09pt, "Electrical measurements were conducted via a costum made ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 487.12pt, "microfluidic cell containing Ag/AgCl electrdoes then using the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 499.12pt, "electrical reader from Elements srl.   Voltage ramps were biased ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 511.12pt, "to one of the Ag/AgCl and the transmembrane ionic current was ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 523.12pt, "recorded through the other Ag/AgCl. Each measurement was ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 535.14pt, "carried out more than three times of Vb scans to obtain the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 547.14pt, "arithmetic average of the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 559.14pt, "ionic current, which was used for the evaluation of the in-pore ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 571.16pt, "reaction- mediated ionic current characteristics .  ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 583.16pt, "All salts were used as received without additional purification: ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 595.16pt, "NaCl (>99.5% purity), CaCl₂ (>95.0% purity), and MnCl₂ (>99.0% ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 607.16pt, "purity) were obtained from Sigma Aldrich. ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 619.19pt, "To avoid cross-contamination and unwanted precipitation ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 631.19pt, "when changing between different electrolyte solutions, the ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 643.19pt, "following cleaning protocol was strictly followed: the existing ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 655.19pt, "solution was completely aspirated from the microfluidic cell ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 667.21pt, "with a pipette, after which both the inlet and outlet channels ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 679.21pt, "were thoroughly rinsed (at least five times) with Milli-Q water. ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 691.21pt, "Only then was the new salt solution introduced. This step is ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 703.21pt, "critical because direct contact between certain electrolyte ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 715.24pt, "combinations (particularly those containing phosphate buffers ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 727.24pt, "and divalent cations) can trigger immediate precipitation of ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 739.24pt, "insoluble salts, which would contaminate the nanopore walls, ")
  #line-at(42.452pt, 751.235pt, "the membrane surface, and the entire fluidic system. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.857pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
